# tier: original-diagnostic
# oracle: independent-derivation
# scenario: diag-stic2-collision-pass
# profile: intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
# program: fixtures/FX-diag-stic-2/diag-stic-2.listing.txt (ivs-diag-stic-2), entered through the
#   project boot stub contract 2 (boot-stub-2: cartridge reset entry 5000, interrupt entry 5004), with
#   the zero graphics ROM and no EXEC image
#
# Predicate of ivs-diag-stic-2 with KEY_5 closed from tick 0, the selector byte BD (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05,
#   D-10): the guest words at the one bound (marker 03C5, the frame counter 000A, the selector word 00BD, the
#   scene number 0009), frame 0 not displayed, frame 4 displayed, the sixteen read-out words of the collision
#   registers (the rows T1 to T16 of the truth table, section (d): sticky bits read in frame 3 after a frame
#   with no overlap, the own bit clear, the interaction bit required, an invisible MOB still interacting, set
#   card and Colored Squares pixels as background, a CPU write of zero clearing, read again in frame 4) masked
#   with 03FF, two pixel probes in frame 5 (a MOB over a Colored Squares block each), and ten delivered frames;
#   no frame hash (the background of the collision frames is not derivable, the program does not write the color
#   stack), all derived by hand in docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md (sections (a) to (f); the frame literals
#   data/video/frames/F-M*.frame with their sha256-text keys) BEFORE the program, its listing, the scenario or
#   any run existed (oracle commit 641a12e3a1059b242cc88a3ee4308e3f58d9b36d, blind second read closed in commit
#   9250265), and copied here line for line from the committed block. It was not generated by, read back from or
#   edited to match the core or a run. The author of this derivation also wrote the literals, the STIC rules,
#   the program and the core, and the blind reader is of the same model family, so all of them can share one
#   misreading of a source; agreement among them is not independent evidence about hardware.
# The read-out words are stored by the routines of frames 3 and 4 and stay unchanged afterwards, so the one
#   bound at tick 640,000 sees them; the two pixel probes are in frame 5, away from any frame of the input or
#   the next. The scenario has no frame tie because the collision frames carry cells that are not derivable (the
#   color stack registers are not written in the collision selector).
# Excluded on purpose: machine time (printed in the report, never asserted), the stack word [0340] (C68),
# all CPU registers, R7 and the flags (C40, C45, C56), and every pinned item of the derivation, section
# (i): the pixels of a MOB with the priority bit set (PD-1), half-height pixels (PD-2), a collision of a MOB
# at X coordinate 0 (PD-3), the border bit of a collision register (PD-4), a collision outside the plane
# (PD-5), a collision in a frame with the display off (PD-6), the read and clear semantics of the collision
# registers beyond sticky bits and a write of zero (PD-7), the height unit of the top strip (PD-8), a strip
# against the delay (PD-9), the content of the area a delay exposes and a MOB in it (PD-10, PD-11), the delay
# range (PD-12), and the bus windows against the vertical delay (PD-13).
# Body: one assert per clause in the runner's scenario grammar, hex upper case, exact compare, evaluated
# at the end of the step above it, in the order of data/scenarios/diag-stic2-collision-pass.ivss
# (golden-expect-drift). The step line below is a comment.
# step: run-to 640000 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000A
assert mem 02F2 == 00BD
assert mem 02F3 == 0009
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 4 displayed == yes
assert mem 0300 == 0002
assert mem 0301 == 0001
assert mem 0302 == 0008
assert mem 0303 == 0004
assert mem 0304 == 0000
assert mem 0305 == 0000
assert mem 0306 == 0100
assert mem 0307 == 0000
assert mem 0308 == 0000
assert mem 0309 == 0100
assert mem 030A == 0100
assert mem 030B == 0000
assert mem 030C..030F == 0000
assert frame 5 pixel 108 52 == 5
assert frame 5 pixel 132 52 == 6
assert video count == 10
